OL,3,GNEWSADonating kidney to daughter a
OL,4,A'no-brainer', says dad
OL,5,
OL,6,FFather-of-two Brad Walker said it was a
OL,7,F"no-brainer" when he found out he could
OL,8,Fdonate his kidney to his five-year-old
OL,9,Fdaughter.
OL,11,FThe 28-year-old, from Chellaston,
OL,12,FDerby, said he "got lucky" to be a
OL,13,Ftransplant match for Noa-Rae, who has
OL,14,Fnephrotic syndrome, a condition which
OL,15,Fcauses the kidneys to leak large
OL,16,Famounts of protein into the urine.
OL,18,FShe was diagnosed at the age of two
OL,19,Fbefore having both kidneys removed a
OL,20,Fyear later and has frequently missed
OL,21,Fschool because of illness.
OL,23,APub: 14-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (E) NewsCReg TVFWeather
